  "slug": "store-use-cases-and-proposals",
  "name": "Store use cases and proposals",
  "description": "The workspace keeps one file per entity: each use case in .lastro/usecases/<id>-<slug>.json (id, slug, name, description, proofs, history) and each proposal in .lastro/proposals/<id>-<slug>.json, with its receipt next to it. Use cases are numbered UC-001, UC-002... and proposals P-001, P-002... with the next free number, never reused even after a removal; intents and proofs are numbered inside their proposal (P-007.I-03, P-007.PF-05) and keep that id when a proof moves to its use case. Slugs are kebab-case and stable: a rename changes only the name. intents.json, spec.json and proof.json are no longer written.",
